%% caption: The big picture. You play in Simitone, which reads your own copy of The Sims 1 from disk and keeps its settings and saves in your Documents folder. Our mod layer rewrites a few parts of the released game after the fact.
flowchart LR
  P(["You, the player"])
  W["Simitone.Windows<br/>starts the game"]
  C["Simitone.Client<br/>menus, screens, buttons"]
  E["FreeSO engine libraries<br/>rules, drawing, file reading"]
  G[("Your Sims 1 install<br/>Program Files (x86)/Maxis/The Sims")]
  D[("Documents/Simitone<br/>settings, saves, mod choices")]
  M["Mod layer (Tools/)<br/>patches the released game"]
  P -->|plays through| C
  W -->|launches| C
  C -->|asks for everything below| E
  E -->|reads objects, houses, sounds from| G
  C -->|keeps settings and saves in| D
  M -->|adds menu and hooks to| C
  M -->|changes how objects are drawn in| E
